  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Assistance to Bagana Volcano Affected Communities in the Autonomous Region of Bougainville, Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 7 July 2023, Mount Bagana, located in the Autonomous Region of Bougainville (AROB) in Papua New Guinea, experienced a moderate volcanic eruption which emitted ashes, gas, and steam plumes and caused significant ashfall in local communities. Two eruptions were reported in the following days by local communities. About 8,000 affected people within the disaster zone are reportedly in need of immediate assistance. Immediate needs identified by the Autonomous Bougainville Government include temporary shelter, non-food items (NFIs) including water containers and water purification tablets, safe and clean drinking water, food rations, medical supplies, and protection services. The need for a detailed sectoral assessment to determine the full extent of the disaster was highlighted.Through this project, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) aims to meet the urgent humanitarian needs of people affected by the moderate volcanic eruption in AROB, particularly vulnerable groups such as older people and people living with disabilities. IOM is scaling up and expanding its existing field presence and portfolio to provide emergency assistance to affected populations, focusing on shelter, NFIs, and camp coordination and camp management. IOM is also providing logistics support to authorities to transport NFIs and deploying field assessment teams.</narrative>
  </description>
